<title>POLAND: BIG sells new issue shares at PLN 3.4.</title>
<headline>BIG sells new issue shares at PLN 3.4.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych SA (BIG) sold 65 million shares of its issue to help refinance the aqcuisition of Bank Gdanski at 3.4 zlotys each, BIG's spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In sum we sold 65 million series I shares at a price of 3.4 zlotys,&quot; Wojciech Kaczorowski told Reuters, adding that GDR manager Merrill Lynch had the option to buy eight million BIG shares from Bank Gdanski.</p>
<p>Kaczorowski said the 20,000,000 shares in the domestic tranche were sold as well as 45 million shares in the GDR tranche and more details would be available later on Tuesday.</p>
<p> Issuer:				   Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych</p>
<p> Type of issue:			  new common shares</p>
<p> Previous Pricing Range (PLN):     3.30-5.30</p>
<p> No of Shares Offered:		 75,000,000</p>
<p> No of Existing Shares:		163,470,872</p>
<p> Lead Domestic Manager:		BIG-BG sp zoo.</p>
<p> GDR Manager:			    Merrill Lynch International</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:		     N.A.</p>
<p> Use Of Proceeds:			refinance acquisition of</p>
<p>					     Bank Gdanski, supporting</p>
<p>					     banks' integration</p>
<p> Tranches		     No of Shares</p>
<p>				  Offered</p>
<p> Domestic		     20,000,000</p>
<p> GDRs			   55,000,000</p>
<p>NOTES: Bank of New York is depositary bank for GDRs and Bank Pekao SA is the custodian bank.</p>
<p>- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
